1b:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Temporary traffic control is governed by the Manual on Uniform Traffic Control Devices, which most states adopt or adapt. It defines the zones a work area is divided into, and the distances between them are calculated from the speed of approaching traffic — not estimated on site."}]
1c:["$","figure","2",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Zone"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Purpose"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Advance warning area"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Tells drivers what is ahead, before they can see it"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Transition area"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Moves traffic out of its normal path, using a taper"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Buffer space"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Empty space giving an errant vehicle room to stop before reaching workers"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Activity area"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Where the work happens"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Termination area"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Returns traffic to normal"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"The parts of a traffic control zone"}]]}]
1d:["$","div","3",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"The buffer space is deliberately empty and it is not storage. Parking a vehicle, stacking materials, or standing in it removes the margin that exists for a driver who is not paying attention. A buffer space being used for anything is one of the clearest signs a work zone is not being run correctly."]}]
1e:["$","figure","4",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Item / signal"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Detail"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"STOP/SLOW paddle"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"The primary device. A red flag is for emergencies only"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"High-visibility apparel"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"ANSI/ISEA 107 Performance Class 2 or 3; the MUTCD says Class 3 should be considered for night work"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"To stop traffic"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Face traffic, hold the STOP face toward them, raise the free arm palm out"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"To let traffic proceed"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Show the SLOW face and motion with the free hand"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"To slow traffic"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Show SLOW and lower the free hand in a slowing motion"}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Escape route"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Planned before work starts — where you go if a vehicle does not stop"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Standard flagging equipment and signals"}]]}]
1f:["$","div","5",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-blue-50 border-blue-400","children":[false,"Two things distinguish a safe flagger station: it is visible to approaching drivers with enough distance to stop, and it is never in the path of traffic. Stand on the shoulder or in a closed lane, not in a live one. And know your escape route before you need it — a flagger who has to decide where to go in the moment does not have time to decide."]}]
20:["$","div","6",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"Flagger training is a separate requirement from OSHA training. In New York, the State DOT requires every flagger on its projects to be trained by a recognized program, such as the American Traffic Safety Services Association (ATSSA), the National Safety Council, or a union or industry training program, and contractors must list their certified flaggers before work starts. Other states and employers set their own rules, and some flagger cards must be renewed. Completing OSHA 30 does not make you a certified flagger, and this coursework does not either."]}]
21:["$","$L25","7",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"What is the buffer space in a work zone for?","options":["Storing equipment and materials close to the work","Empty space giving an errant vehicle room to stop before it reaches workers","Parking for the work crew's vehicles","The area where the flagger stands"],"correctIndex":1,"explanation":"The buffer space exists specifically to be empty. It is the margin for a driver who does not slow or stop in time, and putting anything in it — vehicles, materials, or people — removes the protection it provides.","optionRationales":["Storing materials there defeats its entire purpose.","Correct. It is deliberately empty space.","Parking in the buffer removes the margin and creates a struck-by hazard.","The flagger station is positioned separately, out of the path of traffic."]}}]
22:["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-[40px] sm:leading-[1.05]","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-3 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft","children":"Apply what you've learned in this lesson."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Traffic control is governed by published standards — work from them."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Find the flagger training requirement where you will work: who provides the training, what it costs, and whether the card must be renewed."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Look up the MUTCD taper length formula and calculate the required taper for a 45 mph road."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Find the high-visibility apparel class required for night work on a highway."}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Observe a real work zone from a safe distance and identify each of the five zones. Note anything that does not match the standard."}]]}]]}]}]]}]
